      "title": "README -- V12 UNIFIED SPATIAL",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note",
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "V12 UNIFIED SPATIAL -- quick start\n================================================================\nBoxes control WHERE each subject renders, HOW LARGE it appears, and\nwhich character LoRA owns it. Hover any input for a tooltip.\n\n1. Load the three Krea 2 models (UNet / Qwen3-VL CLIP / VAE) and put the\n   Krea 2 identity edit LoRA in the V12 node's edit_lora slot.\n2. Scene photo: load any photo into the LoadImage wired to extra_ref_1.\n   Your characters are GENERATED INTO that scene (lighting and\n   perspective integrate naturally -- this is not a paste).\n3. Prompt: describe the scene and what the people are doing. Keep\n   \"background is from reference photo 1\" when using a scene photo.\n   Interactions (\"arm around\", \"holding hands\") go here.\n4. Draw one box per character, sized like the person should appear:\n   tall box = close/large subject, small box = distant subject.\n   Short generic box descriptions (\"man\", \"woman\"). Don't overlap.\n5. In the V12 node: pick each row's character LoRA. Strength 1.3-1.4,\n   base_strength 1.1. Region prompts stay short (\"a man\") -- identity\n   comes from the LoRA. Portraits stay OFF.\n6. Optional outfit transfer: load a clothing photo into the LoadImage\n   wired to extra_ref_2 (it is muted by default -- unmute to use) and\n   keep the refs_json role: {\"role\":\"object\",\"note\":\"outfit, worn by\n   the woman\"}.\n7. Detailer: leave enabled for an extra per-subject face + body pass\n   with each region's own LoRA. If furniture inside boxes changes,\n   lower body_denoise to ~0.20.\n8. Sampler is preset for Krea 2 Turbo: euler / 12 steps / CFG 1.\n   First run compiles the fused attention kernel (~1 min, once per\n   session).\n\nIf likeness is weak: raise the row strength before anything else.\nIf identities mix: check box order matches row order, and keep\nblend_override at 0."
      ],
      "color": "#444",
      "bgcolor": "#222"
    },
